UID:93666-1788546600-1788552000@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Gender in the Built Environment
DESCRIPTION:This inaugural discussion launches the Bangalore edition of the exhibition\, “Expanding Agency and Archival Silences”. Panellists will foreground questions of gender and agency within spatial design practices in India\, and lay the foundation for the upcoming walkthroughs\, discussions\, and workshops. Agency is negotiated\, marked\, and expanded in multiple ways. \nIn the current socio-political climate and technological transformation\, why is it important not just to think about it\, but to build practices that expand agency? \nParticularly\, why should it matter to architects\, planners\, and designers? \nWhat tools\, methods\, or frameworks do you recommend for introducing and including diverse voices into the practices of building living environments? \nAcross the five days\, a series of activities brings together conversations\, lived experiences and participatory practices to explore how gender shapes the ways we design\, build\, inhabit\, teach\, and resonate with the ‘space’. Curators will be in conversation with practitioners from across borders to make space for care\, compassion\, responsiveness\, and nuanced understandings of inhabitable spaces for co-existence.  \nEmerging thoughts will pave the path for continued engagements on the subject within the region\, and across borders and disciplinary boundaries.  \nThis event is a part of the “Expanding Agency and Archival Silences” exhibition. Find the full schedule here.  \nIn collaboration with: \n     \n\n\nExpanding Agency and Archival Silences\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf3L1NpKUS1iznO4VnYo8T04sOknCP-w0NBBsVwucCxGoUUTA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Kathleen James-Chakraborty\, Amit Srivastava\, Ranjana Raghunathan\, Krishnapriya Rajshekar\, Madhumati A\, Ishita Shah\, Sarah Melsens\n*Event Categories*: Architecture\, Environment\, Gender\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/gender-in-the-built-environment/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Architecture,Environment,Gender,Visual Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail-opening-panel.png
END:VEVENT
