SUMMARY:Demystifying Trauma
DESCRIPTION:Trauma is a silent epidemic in India\, hiding in plain sight\, embedding itself in our bodies\, families\, and relationships\, and surfacing as anxiety\, addiction\, chronic illness\, and quiet self-doubt that we rarely identify correctly. \nKeeping survivor testimonies and science at the forefront\, this panel discussion\, based on the book Trauma Nation: Fighting India’s Silent Epidemic\, will unpack how trauma travels through childhood\, relationships\, historical events such as Partition\, and even our news feeds\, and also explore why it so often goes unrecognised and unnamed. \nHow do we identify trauma when it hides behind everyday anxieties\, addictions\, and illnesses? And what might healing look like in the Indian context? \nPresented by:\n \nVenue: Library\n\n\nA Research-Driven Conversation on Pain\, Memory\, and Healing\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfnB8LkEvC14LWx_b0jjLsnWbgPaOqrp27zotAWqS3MyxSARg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Nishtha Lamba\, Amandeep Sandhu\, Pavitra Jayaraman\n*Event Categories*: Health & Wellness\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/demystifying-trauma/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_DT.jpg
